Session 01 was what we thought would be one-shot with Brad, Casey-B, and Jasper, and took place in a desert of Calimshan.

Brad's character is a Calimite Tabaxi/Half-elf cross (Cat person) named Shamsii Kafa Niyaz al-Milh. He's nimble, outspoken and proud (a formible warrior and sailor as well)

Casey's character is Moru, a half-orc Monk of the Way of the Long Death, a wanderer from the North. She is hard-eyed, terrifying, and frankly lacks all and any qualities that could be called "people skills".

Jasper's character for the one-shot was Hasseid. A Calimite, human cleric. (He did not continue with this character)

The three found themselves together, all captured independently as slaves, and being carted across the sands of the Calim desert.

They were held among a caravan of slaves owned by the local Calif, and were being taken from the main estate to one where the Calif holidayed for lack of a better term.

Meanwhile, one of the Calif's harem, a young girl, had been plotting her escape. She had recently discovered she was pregnant, and was not, as one of the proper wives of the calif, going to be allowed to keep her child should the wives and the Calif discover the coming of her child.

She had enlisted another Tabaxi, one of the Calif's Harem guard to help her escape, he had fallen in love with her in secret.

On the journey to the estate, the Tabaxi and the young mother-to-be took the opportunity to break free of the guards and the caravan.

Our session started with well basically a magical grenade landing in a slave cart where my three players found themselves, which exploded and sent the card barrelling down a dune!

The players fought off several slavers, struggling to free themselves and taking advantage of the chaos, and once they managed to best their immediate opponents/captors saw in the distance a young woman riding with her robes streaming behind her, galloping at great speed away from the caravan, followed by a mounted Tabaxi, and both being pursued by a dozen men on horseback.

It was great fun and one of the best openings I've ever pulled off. Very cinematic and a fun way to just dive in.

Anyway, the players followed the tracks across the desert and found several knuckle-shaped plateaus, around which were oasis, and interestingly many horses parked. After some exploring they found a cave with a large chamber within. Slumped against a stone was the Tabaxi, slumped against of the stones dotting the chamber floor. An ornate urn sat before a curious and ominous circular carving on the chamber's far wall.

As they investigated, they found the Tabaxi was hanging on to life, barely, but was unconscious. Before they had time to get their bearings, a misty figure emerged from the Urn.

Mysterous Djinn dialog occurred to the effect of, if you pass these three challenges, I will free you.

1) was a fight with a bone naga,
2) Was a fight with a pair of shades that guarded a portal gateway the genie opened,
and
3) "wait, what's the third thing?" said one of the players after the portal was clear, the throneroom of the Calif's estate shimmering on the other side... "Save the child", said the Djinn.

Haha. A fight ensued to save the young woman, who was about to be executed for her insolance, and we ended right before the players would have had to figure out how to escape and get her (and themselves) to safety.

For our current players, Brad and Casey B, this was their first adventure as their characters and the in-between story we reckoned from there was that they stayed on the run, got the young woman to safety, reunited with the Lover tabaxi, and found their way onto a ship as crew members, and for the last 3 years or so, sailed together as crew for whatever ships would need the help, becoming skilled sailors and watching eachother's backs.